# Expectation record for 12_preprocessor/004_predefined_macros.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 004_predefined_macros
area               = 12_preprocessor
description        = Predefined macros asserted only as normalized relations: the standard conformance and version macros, source-position macros, architecture-macro consistency, and the tie between the preprocessor's view of the target and the code generator's pointer width
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour. The only arithmetic is a bounded
increment over the characters of a string literal and a sum of four operands each of which is 0 or 1,
so no signed overflow is reachable. No shift operator appears, so no shift count can be out of range.
There is no cast between object pointer types, no union and no type-punning, so no aliasing rule is
stressed. The helper walks a string literal and stops at its terminator, so no pointer is formed past
the end of an object and none is dereferenced outside one; no string literal is modified. Every object
is initialized at its declaration. No object is modified twice between sequence points. Every call
receives a single argument that has no side effect at all, so nothing depends on unspecified
evaluation order.

DETERMINISM. Every printed value is an int printed with %d or a string constant written in this
source, so nothing target-varying, address-derived, time-derived, random or locale-dependent can
reach stdout. No plain char value is printed: char signedness was measured as signed on x86_64 and
i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64, so a plain-char value would diverge for a reason that is
not a defect. No raw type width is printed: sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) were measured as 4 on
i686 and 8 on the other three targets. Iteration order is fixed by literal bounds. main returns 0,
inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is truncated.

HERMETICITY. Every input is a literal in this source. Nothing is opened, nothing is read from the
environment, the command line, the clock or the file system, and no storage is allocated, so a cell
is reproducible from this source and this record alone.

GATE. The default warning gate applies unmodified and no `ub_audit_flags` key appears:
-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror. The program was verified
clean under that gate with all four reference drivers and with the alternate reference compiler, and
it builds and runs clean under -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both gates are
reference-compiler-only and are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is
untouched.

NO HEADER IS INCLUDED and printf is declared by hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`. bcc bundles
only freestanding headers and ships no standard I/O header, so naming one would fail on the bcc side
of oracle (a) while succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious divergence caused by the test
rather than by a compiler.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
WHICH MACROS MAY BE ASSERTED AS INVARIANTS, AND WHICH MAY NOT. This is the whole design of the
program, and it is a soundness requirement rather than a stylistic preference.

Only macros the C standard itself requires are invariants here: __STDC__ and __STDC_VERSION__ (C11
6.10.8.1), and the source-position macros __LINE__ and __FILE__ (same clause). A conforming
implementation must define each of them, so a divergence in one is a real conformance gap and a
legitimate finding.

The architecture macros are NOT invariants, and an earlier form of this program wrongly made them one
by asserting that exactly one of __x86_64__, __i386__, __aarch64__ and __riscv is defined. Those are
spellings of a particular compiler family; no clause obliges any implementation to define them, and
this repository documents no per-target predefined-macro contract for the compiler under test. That
assertion would therefore have accused a correct compiler of a defect merely for spelling its
architecture macro differently, or for leaving the choice to a target header. They are still
exercised, because dropping them would be excluding a feature for being awkward, but only through
assertions no correct compiler can fail: that NO MORE THAN ONE of the four is defined, which is a
consistency property rather than a naming one, and that ANY macro that IS defined agrees with the
pointer width the code generator actually produced, written as a two-sided implication so that an
undefined macro satisfies it vacuously. Together those still catch the defect worth catching -- a
preprocessor that disagrees with its own back end, or that claims two architectures at once -- while a
differently spelled or absent macro set passes.

The strict-conformance macro is asserted NOWHERE, in either direction, for the same reason:
__STRICT_ANSI__ is a compiler-family spelling with no standard mandate, so requiring its absence would
be a false oracle and requiring its presence would be another. Whether GNU extensions are on offer is
exercised where it belongs, in feature area 08, by programs that USE an extension.

WIDTH NORMALIZATION. No macro value and no type width is printed as an absolute. The one place a width
appears is inside a relation, `sizeof(void *) == 4u`, whose truth value is compared against an
architecture macro rather than printed, and `sizeof(void *) == sizeof(long)`, which is a genuine
four-target invariant even though the shared value differs between the 32-bit target and the other
three. The line-number macro is reduced to positivity and the file-name macro to non-emptiness, so no
workspace path can reach the output and no later edit to the comments above can change a printed
value.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
stdc_is_one=1
stdc_at_least_c99=1
stdc_at_least_c11=1
arch_count_at_most_one=1
arch_id_agrees_with_pointer_width=1
pointer_width_eq_long_width=1
line_macro_positive=1
file_macro_nonempty=1
END
